1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,600
Please stand, that's fine. Speaking of the final episode, I want to say that it's not just the two girls who don't want it to end.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,840
Now that we've reached the final episode, let's invite one more person to say goodbye. Boom? Oh, sorry, no.

3
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:16,720
No, we haven't greeted the people upstairs yet. Come on, everyone upstairs, say bye-bye! Bye!

4
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:20,960
The sound from upstairs is really quiet. It's so quiet; we can't hear you down here.

5
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,560
[Cheering] Can you hear them?

6
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:27,199
Can you see us upstairs? We'll get to you in a moment.

7
00:00:27,199 --> 00:00:35,879
We can't see you or hear you. If you can't hear us, how can you answer? Yeah, that's true. How does that work? Anyway, what I was saying is, today...

8
00:00:35,879 --> 00:00:41,760
The tickets were so hard to get. They sold out in no time because the fans wanted to come...

9
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:46,879
...and watch the final episode with Lena and Miu. But now, let's talk about this episode. Please welcome...

10
00:00:46,879 --> 00:00:54,680
...one more person, someone who has worked so hard behind the scenes and made everything happen. P'Ao! P'Ao!

11
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:58,160
Where is P'Ao, our producer? P'Ao! Where is Khun Patchanee?

12
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:04,839
Where is P'Ao? Patchanee! She's here, she's here! There she is. Let's hear it for her!

13
00:01:04,839 --> 00:01:10,560
Make some noise! [Cheering] Come on, let's go!

14
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:13,414
You know her, right? [Cheering]

15
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:18,360
Here she comes, our director!

16
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:28,960
Careful, P'Ao, you might fall! Don't rush. You're not going to fall. [Music] Come over here.

17
00:01:32,354 --> 00:01:34,375
[Music]

18
00:01:40,216 --> 00:01:45,158
[Music] Hello, P'Ao! P'Ao said she's feeling shy.

19
00:01:45,158 --> 00:01:49,479
There are so many people here! And the reason it's so packed is because...

20
00:01:49,479 --> 00:01:52,439
...they want to celebrate P'Ao's and the girls' success.

21
00:01:52,439 --> 00:01:55,439
They want to see my success! They also want to see your girls.

22
00:01:55,439 --> 00:01:59,960
And you were behind it all, too. So, P'Ao, how does it feel? Let me ask you, as the producer...

23
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:05,200
...now that we've made it all the way to the final episode. Can we get both of them to come up front?

24
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:10,399
Yes. I was worried that if I stood right here, too close to them, the fans wouldn't be able to take photos...

25
00:02:10,399 --> 00:02:15,680
...of Miu because I'd end up blocking her face. And if I stood over here, I'd block you instead. So I was trying to move...

26
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:20,879
...people around. How's that? What was the question again? [Laughter]

27
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:25,680
How does it feel now that we've reached the final episode? Honestly, I'm excited. I can't believe we're already at the final...

28
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,720
...episode. It went by so quickly. Yes.

29
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:33,160
And I still can't believe that we've come all this way, from the very first day...

30
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:37,239
...until today. We've all been through so much together.

31
00:02:37,239 --> 00:02:42,599
We believe that the people watching at home have only seen half of what we've experienced...

32
00:02:42,599 --> 00:02:49,239
...and what we've seen ourselves. Then why don't we show them everything?

33
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:56,920
I'd like to thank everyone who has supported the girls and supported this project from the very beginning...

34
00:02:56,920 --> 00:03:01,040
...all the way until today. Some of you have been with us since Safe Zone, too.

35
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:06,159
Thank you so much. Let's hear it for her! [Applause] And now, let's hear from the girls.

36
00:03:06,159 --> 00:03:11,560
Speaking of the characters, today we're saying goodbye to them. Is there anything you'd like to say...

37
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:17,519
...to these two characters, Pim and Pa? What would you like to tell them, after being with them...

38
00:03:17,519 --> 00:03:21,319
...since the very beginning? Do I have to say it now? P'Mew, you can speak. You can save it for the end.

39
00:03:21,319 --> 00:03:23,760
Please, can I? I don't want to make everyone cry.

40
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:30,560
Yes, don't say it now. P'Ao, I could lend you my sleeve, but I'm afraid it won't be enough. You'll need mine, too!

41
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:33,840
Can I have a tissue, please? Oh!

42
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:40,319
Okay, okay, let's save that for later. Let P'Ao speak first.

43
00:03:41,519 --> 00:03:48,159
Can't I? Then, P'Nung, tell us about the characters we've nurtured since day one.

44
00:03:48,159 --> 00:03:54,000
Filming wasn't just a matter of shooting for eight days and wrapping up. These characters really put us through it, didn't they, P'Wu?

45
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,640
Let's start with you. We were there from the beginning, when we didn't even know what the team would be like yet.

46
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:06,920
We gradually learned about one another, how everyone worked, and how each person's pace and way of speaking were.

47
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:16,880
We saw Pa when she was still doing really well, and then, once filming began, we saw how difficult her life had become...

48
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:26,240
...and how she slowly developed from being at rock bottom to finally getting back on her feet. And now, you can see where she is.

49
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:31,228
That's what everyone has seen today. [Applause]

50
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:37,039
Are you ready to talk about the characters?

51
00:04:37,039 --> 00:04:40,280
Go ahead. Do you want to talk about them? It's completely up to you.

52
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:46,238
It's entirely up to you. If you're afraid you'll cry, I'll skip the question. Can we skip it for now?

53
00:04:46,238 --> 00:04:47,520
[Laughter] Let's skip it.

54
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:52,080
She's really attached to them. I understand. Sometimes, when you've spent so much time filming...

55
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:56,320
...you end up falling in love with the characters.

56
00:04:56,320 --> 00:05:04,880
Yes. On the first day we went to read the script, I thought, "Wow, this character is so cute and tiny."

57
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:11,680
Was that just you acting, or did you really feel that way? Yes, she's so fun to play. Can we start filming yet?

58
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,680
Today? Uh...

59
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:20,880
And when we finally went to shoot, it was so much fun. P'Ru, playing this character was really immersive.

60
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:24,400
We fell in love with the character, and the character became part of us. We gave ourselves to the character, and the character gave something back to us.

61
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:30,639
I got excited along with the character, too. Oh, I really love this series. I was like...

62
00:05:30,639 --> 00:05:34,108
Really? [Laughter]

63
00:05:34,759 --> 00:05:42,680
I have to say, there are things I wouldn't do. So let me ask: was there any scene during filming that you found especially difficult?

64
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,639
The hardest scene? "Spread your legs."

65
00:05:45,639 --> 00:05:50,240
Like... The "spread your legs" scene.

66
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,600
Wait...

67
00:05:54,039 --> 00:05:59,080
The "spread your legs" scene? [Laughter] Whose legs are we talking about? We couldn't even get through reading it—let alone filming it!

68
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:04,560
From the very first script reading, we couldn't say "spread your legs" out loud. It was so awkward.

69
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:10,080
Why? Even Farang had to repeat it: "Spread your legs." [Laughter]

70
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:13,720
I couldn't read it. "Spread your legs."

71
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:16,479
"Spread your legs." Why? What's wrong?

72
00:06:16,479 --> 00:06:24,720
I just couldn't say it. I couldn't do it. P'Boom, when someone conservative like me comes across something like this...

73
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:30,440
...it's a shock. It's a culture shock. I was thinking, "I would never do this."

74
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:36,800
I was like, "No way!" when I read it. But when the actual filming day came, there were certain key words...

75
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:44,759
...that I discussed with the director, and then I just went for it. Maybe it was because, as this character...

76
00:06:44,759 --> 00:06:50,360
...I was playing the younger one who brings everyone happiness in the story, you know?

77
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:55,280
We were selling the idea of spending time together, but there wasn't any physical contact, so it was different.

78
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:57,800
Right. Was there a scene that you felt you absolutely couldn't do?

79
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:02,360
There was only one. It was this scene.

80
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:06,440
That was the hardest "spread your legs" scene for me. Because with action scenes, sometimes...

81
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:11,960
...it's not embarrassing. I mean, doing it with P'Inna is fine. But when you actually have to say those words...

82
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:19,479
...as part of an action you have to perform, it feels embarrassing and uncomfortable. Saying the words is awkward.

83
00:07:19,479 --> 00:07:25,599
Okay, because in that scene you're sitting on someone's lap, and Farang is sitting behind you. Then Farang says...

84
00:07:25,599 --> 00:07:29,280
"Spread your legs." "Spread your legs."

85
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:34,000
And then P'Kook wouldn't do it! [Laughter]

86
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,000
But in the end, it all worked out. I'd say that was the hardest thing for me.

87
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,440
Oh, it wasn't that hard when we actually filmed it. It wasn't as difficult as reading it. P'Ao made it easier because...

88
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:49,599
...she only gave us 20 minutes. Exactly. We had no choice but to just go for it.

89
00:07:49,599 --> 00:07:54,680
She said, "Don't say anything. Just do it, do it! We're running out of time, and the crew needs to wrap up."

90
00:07:54,680 --> 00:08:00,280
P'Ao was going to say, "Please help Mom, darling." [Screaming] No!

91
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:06,000
Everyone just gave it their all. And what about you, Lena? Was there a scene you found really difficult?

92
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:14,360
A really difficult one? The dramatic scenes? Oh, but we're great at drama! Was it really that hard? Which scene?

93
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:22,720
I think the scenes where the character has to feel shy are difficult, especially when the character has to hide her feelings.

94
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:27,840
Of course, dramatic scenes are difficult, too. But the scene where she puts on the apron...

95
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:34,240
...that scene was so embarrassing. It was really embarrassing, but Pim couldn't show that she was flustered.

96
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:40,000
So it created this tension. I wanted to smile, but I couldn't. I had to keep Pim's expression straight...

97
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:44,519
...and keep a straight face the whole time. That's why...

98
00:08:44,519 --> 00:08:51,519
...it felt so awkward. Honestly, I wanted to show how I really felt. If I were playing myself, I would have jumped...

99
00:08:51,519 --> 00:08:56,279
...right into it. But when I was Pim, I had to hold back.

100
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:01,279
"The food doesn't taste good," or something like that. Yeah, just a little bit of acting there.

101
00:09:01,279 --> 00:09:04,200
Honestly, the hardest scenes are the ones where we have to hold back our real emotions.

102
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,079
Exactly. Oh!

103
00:09:05,079 --> 00:09:08,079
Hey, what do you mean? [Laughter] You have to keep your emotions in check.

104
00:09:08,079 --> 00:09:13,279
Keep your emotions in check. But hold on a moment. Please put your cameras away. The staff can see who's livestreaming.

105
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:18,760
Excuse me, everyone. If you're holding up your phones and livestreaming right now...

106
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:25,760
...please stop livestreaming. Thank you, everyone. We really appreciate your cooperation.

107
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:32,160
All right, let's continue. We need to switch gears a little because some people came here specifically...

108
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:38,240
...for this exclusive experience, and we're livestreaming it right now. The people who couldn't get tickets...

109
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:42,920
...would be disappointed. They went to so much effort for these two, and we shouldn't take advantage of that.

110
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:47,560
We can't do that. If you really love the girls, please don't do it. Don't, okay?

111
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:52,839
So modern! [Sigh] Very modern indeed. Now, speaking of the filming...

112
00:09:52,839 --> 00:10:00,040
...and the challenges involved, was there any scene that really touched you or left an impression? P'Ao, was there one?

113
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:07,320
Was there a scene you filmed and thought, "I really love this! I'm so proud of this work"?

114
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:10,120
I love... So many scenes!

115
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:16,680
You can't tell us about the ending scene! Oh, you like the ending scene? Then you won't have to say anything... Wait, I don't know!

116
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:23,760
That makes it pretty hard for the host to continue! But really, when you're working on a project...

117
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:29,120
...you have to love almost every scene, because if we don't love them, the audience will never love them either.

118
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,000
...at all. Mm-hmm.

119
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,800
So there may be some scenes that feel more special than others, such as the scene where Dee cries...

120
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:40,279
...with tears in her eyes. Mm-hmm.

121
00:10:40,279 --> 00:10:46,839
And the scene where the two of them get married on the bed. Even though it was a very short scene...

122
00:10:46,839 --> 00:10:52,680
...it clearly showed how much these two love each other. We never actually hear this woman say "I love you," but...

123
00:10:52,680 --> 00:11:00,560
...everything she does, every second of her life, is devoted to just one woman.

124
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:06,480
And I have to say, I love every scene. I think the cinematography is so beautiful.

125
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:11,440
We have to thank the crew for that. The visuals in this series are gorgeous. The fans really...

126
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:19,120
...get their money's worth. Just look at the camera angles and the shots. They're absolutely stunning. Even with Meitu...

127
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:23,920
...we couldn't make ourselves look that good! Seriously, everyone can see how soft and beautiful the images are, right?

128
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:29,399
You're praising it too much! No, I'm serious. I watched it and thought, "Wow, even my nose looks so...

129
00:11:29,399 --> 00:11:33,399
...perfectly sculpted, with no shadows, and I still don't look this beautiful and soft!" You know what I mean?

130
00:11:33,399 --> 00:11:36,399
There are techniques involved. We have our techniques. Right?

131
00:11:36,399 --> 00:11:40,480
Exactly. It's premium. Premium! We just...

132
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:44,279
We need a premium membership for that. Yes, yes, because our girls look beautiful in every shot.

133
00:11:44,279 --> 00:11:46,959
Right. So that's a secret.

134
00:11:46,959 --> 00:11:52,240
Yes, it's premium. But honestly, every scene is beautiful. Sometimes, when you're filming a drama...

135
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:57,360
...it's the little scenes that really touch people. They grow into these bigger scenes that stay with everyone.

136
00:11:57,360 --> 00:12:03,079
And what about you, Lena and Miu? Was there a scene that really touched you?

137
00:12:03,079 --> 00:12:09,079
Oh, the touch scene? The touch scene? Yes, the one you really liked and found memorable.

138
00:12:09,079 --> 00:12:12,440
In this series. Oh, the one you liked. Right.

139
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:16,480
Maybe the crew can put it up on the screen for us. Was that the scene we were briefed about?

140
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:19,519
No, I mean, were we supposed to talk about our favorite scene? Is that right?

141
00:12:19,519 --> 00:12:24,360
Yes. A scene and a sequence mean the same thing, darling.

142
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:27,800
I didn't know that! That's why I said maybe they'd show us a picture...

143
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:33,760
P'Ao was probably thinking, "You're really setting me up here!" A scene and a sequence mean the same thing.

144
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:39,880
I was about to say, "I'm sorry." Okay, do you have a scene that you really love?

145
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:42,600
Yes, I do. Oh, then you can answer!

146
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:46,639
Now I know which one, because I've already thought it through carefully...

147
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:50,600
...and it's this scene. There are actually several scenes to choose from, because...

148
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:54,440
...they prepared a few in case you wanted to change your mind about which one to talk about.

149
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:58,920
I actually prepared four scenes, but the one I want to talk about is one I can't mention...

150
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:03,680
...because it's in the final episode. Oh, here we go again!

151
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:10,160
I'm serious! I'm not teasing you. Can we show it? Miu, can we show it?

152
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:13,120
Can we? We can, but they'll blur everything out.

153
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:17,920
We can show it, right? Are we allowed to show it?

154
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:22,160
Do you want to see it? You do, right?

155
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,560
No, I don't! Yes, you do!

156
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:26,760
There it is, there it is! Oh, that's right!

157
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:33,639
This is the picture I chose. Just a moment. Who...

158
00:13:33,639 --> 00:13:38,199
...is it? Um, who made this picture? Did you borrow a premium account?

159
00:13:38,199 --> 00:13:40,880
P'Ao, too! That way the picture will be clearer.

160
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:45,560
Everyone, this is Miu's favorite scene in the series, because it has such a meaningful...

161
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:56,440
...impact. What can you see? I can't see it. I can see sand. I really like the sand in this scene.

162
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:59,360
This is the scene that left an impression on me, but it's in the final episode.

163
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:03,720
Exactly. I want to talk about it, but I can't. If I tell you, there's no point watching it tonight!

164
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,639
We have to watch it together, so let's keep it to ourselves for now.

165
00:14:05,639 --> 00:14:09,440
Yes, let's keep it in our hearts. Oh, that's deep!

166
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:15,680
Very deep, very deep. Let's move on. And what about you, Lena? Do you have a scene...

167
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,959
Which scene? I picked about three scenes, but this one...

168
00:14:19,959 --> 00:14:28,040
...shows the depth of both characters. It's the scene where they clink glasses in episode one.

169
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,240
Yes. Mm-hmm.

170
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:34,320
Can we see it? Let's have a little look. The scene where they clink glasses? This one?

171
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:40,480
Yes. It was really difficult because when we played them, we were used to the version of Pim and Pa...

172
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:44,480
...who had already been through so much together. But we had to go back and play episode one again...

173
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:49,199
...when we didn't know each other's backgrounds yet. There was this desire, this feeling that...

174
00:14:49,199 --> 00:14:52,680
...we wanted the other person so badly that night, you know?

175
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:56,959
It was... Fresh, you know?

176
00:14:56,959 --> 00:15:00,440
Did you see that star just now? For every scene, we need to have a clear objective...

177
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:05,480
...otherwise the scene won't work. So I set my objective as: I want you so badly...

178
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:12,480
...and I'll do whatever it takes to have you right in the palm of my hand. Wait, what do you mean by that?

179
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:17,680
What do you mean? How are you going to do that? You want to unwrap it like...

180
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:23,360
...a brand-new present, like a gift you can't wait to open and see what's inside. Exactly. P'Beam and P'Ao used that exact phrase. They said it was like...

181
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:26,600
...a brand-new gift that we really wanted to unwrap. Oh!

182
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:31,160
So it had to feel like we wanted it so badly, but at the same time...

183
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:37,440
...there had to be a certain softness, a gentleness. It couldn't be too forceful; it had to happen gradually.

184
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,600
Right. Yes, we couldn't just make it too intense or...

185
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,639
...too aggressive. Exactly.

186
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:45,560
So this scene was one where I felt...

187
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:50,519
...the emotions came across really well. It had so many layers. Whether it was Pim...

188
00:15:50,519 --> 00:15:55,440
...or Pa, each of them had their own little tricks and ways of flirting. I felt that it was...

189
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:59,800
...a very nuanced scene. You have to go back and watch it again, right?

190
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:05,120
I believe everyone has watched this scene many times. Trust me!

191
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:08,079
How many times have you watched it? You've been caught!

192
00:16:08,079 --> 00:16:12,040
How many times? How many times? Four or five times?

193
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:14,120
One hundred. One hundred times!

194
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:19,959
